# Deterministic fuse detector (tools/printcheck fusecheck), run on the SLICED
# STL. The production part is a monolith by design — the springs ARE the
# slider-frame connection — so a raw body count proves nothing. Drop the
# chamber (everything +Y of the stop bar: both flexures, the chamber walls,
# the far bar) and require the remainder to fall into 2 separable bodies:
# frame + slider. The remainder still carries every slide-path joint — the
# channel, the deck capture, the knob slot, the tongue window — so a weld
# anywhere on that path survives the drop and reads 1.
#
# flexure zone: y in [46, 200] (2 mm past the stop bar's +Y face, through
# past the far bar), x in [-25.2, 67.6], z in [-0.1, 11.7] (STL coordinates
# as drawn; render.sh does not recenter).
flexure -25.2,46,-0.1:67.6,200,11.7
assert czs-slider.stl 2
# The coupon's seven bodies: the three fit-cell frames, their three FREE
# sliders (each standing stop_clear off its label wall — iteration 1 caught
# them seam-welded at zero gap, which read as 4) and the spring-tethered
# feeler monolith.
assert czs-slider-coupon.stl 7
# Known-fused control: every clearance turned into 0.2 mm interference.
control fused 1
